  "body": "The maintainer reported this in chat on 2026-11-15, on v0.21.0, with a screenshot of the tool editor (End mill, D 8 mm, holder D 44 mm x 35 mm).\n\nHis words: \"tool has a body, but both body and spun profile is overlapping and the spun profile is not \"overriden\" by the toolbody\"\n\n## What happens\n\nThe tool has a body (\"body: drawn profile\", placed from 60.0 mm to 112.0 mm above the tip). The side preview of the tool editor draws the body (orange outline) and also the spun profile from the parameters (the grey holder box). The two shapes overlap. It is not clear which shape the tool uses.\n\n## Expected\n\nWhen a tool has a body, the body replaces the spun profile for the part of the tool that it covers. The preview shows only the shape that the tool uses. The same rule applies to each other view of the tool (the viewport and the simulation), if they draw the two shapes.\n\n## For the work\n\n1. Find which shape the collision check and the simulation use when a body is set. State it in the PR.\n2. Make the preview show the same shape that the collision check uses.\n3. If the collision check uses the parameter holder and not the body (or the opposite) in a way that the user cannot see, file a separate defect issue.\n\nRelated: #743 (bodies as a spun profile).\n\n## Done means\n\n- A tool with a body shows the body and no overlapping parameter holder in the tool editor preview.\n- A tool without a body shows the spun profile as before.\n- A UI test pins the two cases.\n",
